1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,246
Freelancers do not lose money because they invoice badly.

2
00:00:04,197 --> 00:00:07,972
They lose it because chasing a client is unbearable.

3
00:00:07,972 --> 00:00:11,788
Kindly is an agent that does the asking — and closes.

4
00:00:12,410 --> 00:00:15,307
This is a working studio's book.

5
00:00:15,257 --> 00:00:19,073
Eight thousand three hundred fifty dollars outstanding.

6
00:00:19,073 --> 00:00:21,691
Three invoices past due.

7
00:00:21,691 --> 00:00:25,164
Nine hundred already collected through PayPal.

8
00:00:25,164 --> 00:00:34,795
The mandate is the product: two contacts a week, never below seventy
percent up front, no discount without asking, three instalments inside

9
00:00:35,399 --> 00:00:40,506
Acme's accounts-payable agent can release twelve hundred dollars
without a human.

10
00:00:40,456 --> 00:00:43,536
Kindly wants sixteen eighty up front.

11
00:00:43,536 --> 00:00:51,655
Their counter breaks the seventy percent floor, so the policy engine
refuses it automatically — no model involved — and Kindly holds.

12
00:00:51,655 --> 00:00:54,956
Their agent escalates to its finance lead.

13
00:00:54,956 --> 00:00:58,272
Both sides stop where a human should stop.

14
00:00:58,272 --> 00:01:01,456
Every envelope is signed and verified.

15
00:01:02,079 --> 00:01:04,647
Their finance lead approves.

16
00:01:04,597 --> 00:01:11,703
Kindly issues the deferred seven hundred twenty dollars as two dated
PayPal invoices, each with its own payer link.

17
00:01:15,349 --> 00:01:18,549
The parent invoice stays the receivable.

18
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:24,263
Instalments are dated obligations under it, not new debt — the books
do not double count.

19
00:01:24,263 --> 00:01:27,525
And every one is a real PayPal invoice.

20
00:01:28,139 --> 00:01:31,760
The client gets one signed link, and no account.

21
00:01:31,710 --> 00:01:35,183
They can ask for different terms in their own words.

22
00:01:35,183 --> 00:01:40,973
Kindly reads the intent, checks it against the mandate, and answers in
the studio's voice.

23
00:01:41,599 --> 00:01:47,813
When the money lands, the capture comes back as a signed webhook, and
the invoice closes itself.

24
00:01:48,390 --> 00:01:51,682
The ledger records what actually caused it.

25
00:01:51,632 --> 00:01:56,487
Here: paid on their own, ten days early — and Kindly takes no credit.

26
00:01:56,487 --> 00:02:00,632
The same ledger holds the refusal, with the rule it broke.

27
00:02:00,632 --> 00:02:05,645
That is the difference between an agent you can audit, and one you
have to trust.

28
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:09,710
Delegate the ask, not just the reminder.

29
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:15,237
Kindly chases, negotiates and settles through PayPal — and shows you
exactly why.

